      "text": "To solve the equation \\(23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2\\), we will break it down step by step.\n\n1. Calculate \\(23^2\\):\n\n\\[\n23^2 = 23 \\times 23 = 529\n\\]\n\n2. Calculate \\(2(23)(2)\\):\n\n\\[\n2(23)(2) = 46\n\\]\n\n3. Calculate \\(2^2\\):\n\n\\[\n2^2 = 4\n\\]\n\nNow we need to add all these values together:\n\n\\[\n23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2 = 529 + 46 + 4\n\\]\n\nPerform the addition step by step:\n\n\\[\n529 + 46 = 575\n\\]\n\nThen:\n\n\\[\n575 + 4 = 579\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2\\) is \\(\\boxed{579}\\).",
